title: All Have Sinned – None Righteous, No, Not One
description: All have sinned and come short of the glory of God, Jew and Gentile alike, and so we need to be saved.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-salvation-all-have-sinned.html
highlight: sinned; sinneth; sinner; righteous

# Built from the author's teachings under "All have sinned" in studies/data/topics/salvation.json,
# with related teachings on the same theme (6854, 11308, 14018, 17149, 11083, 17871, 10747).
# The slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed.

=== The doctrine
# from 17503
--- All Have Sinned [title]
overline: Doctrine · Salvation
heading: All Have Sinned
sub: We are all sinners before a holy God.
refs: Romans 3:23; Romans 3:10; Ecclesiastes 7:20
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the study. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 6854, 14018
--- Come short of the glory of God
kicker: The doctrine
big: Romans 3:23
lead: The Bible says all have sinned, and so we need to be saved. We need Christ to be the sacrifice, the sole propitiation for our sin.
p: News flash, you aren’t good enough. No one is. We all fall short of the glory of God.

# from 17714, 10747
--- None righteous, no, not one
kicker: Psalm 14 · Romans 3
scripture: Romans 3:10-12
lead: The opening 3 verses of **Psalm 14** stand as the definitive and true statements of the doctrine that all men have sinned and fallen short of the glory of God.
p: It serves as a universal appeal to the need for the gospel, and the reconciliation of fallen men with a holy God. There is none good but God. All have gone astray.
refs: Psalm 14:1-3

# from 17714, 10747
--- The fool hath said
big: Psalm 14:1
p: The opening verse is an even deeper truth, showing the self-deception that leads fools to claim there is no God. They may say this, but ultimately every man knows that God is, and the judge of all things.
p: Those teaching men false doctrines, their words are like the stench of death, of an open grave, because that is what their false gospel brings. It is poison. [[Romans 3:13]] [[Matthew 23:27-28]]

# from 17503
--- Not a just man upon earth
kicker: Ecclesiastes 7
big: Ecclesiastes 7:20
lead: This wisdom is the foundation of the gospel. We are all sinners before a holy God. So even in appearance of righteousness, we have sin. Even in the strength of wisdom, we’ve all done foolishly.
p: An honest inventory, examining ourselves as we are instructed to do, reveals that we too have fallen short. We have cursed others. We have held hatred in our hearts. We have dealt unfairly, the iniquity we see in the wicked has had a home in our hearts.

# from 10736
--- Jew and Gentile alike
kicker: Romans 3
scripture: Romans 3:9
lead: Are they any better than the Gentiles, even with their advantage of having the law? No. In no wise.
p: Because as he’s already proven, all are under sin. All deserve death and Hell. All need salvation. None have any excuse. None have any natural advantage against the judgment of God, which is righteous and just.
callout: The righteousness of God isn’t dependent on our righteousness and isn’t undone by our unrighteousness. Let God be true, but every man a liar. [[Romans 3:4]]

=== Where sin comes from
# from 10792
--- By one man sin entered
kicker: Romans 5
scripture: Romans 5:12
p: The first law was to Adam, and it was simple. And Adam broke the single law in paradise. And by his sin, death came upon the world.
p: And so the law came, so that man had to know that the holiness of God was unattainable by their works, and that faith in His grace alone was our only hope.
refs: Romans 5:20-21

# from 10792, 17149, 15976
--- Not original sin
panel-warn: Original sin | The idea that babies are born guilty, and if they die they go to hell, was created to keep people going to the Roman Catholic apostate Church.
panel: The answer | This is not original sin. There is no sin that follows man from birth, but only the understanding that it is in our nature, even under perfect conditions as Eden, that we still fall short.
callout-honest: As soon as you are water baptizing babies because moms are freaked out about being told that if their kids die, they might go to Hell, you’ve put faith in a rite and a priest and a church. Not Jesus. And not a just God.

# from 12858, 14250
--- No knowledge between good and evil
kicker: Deuteronomy 1 · Romans 7
scripture: Deuteronomy 1:39; Romans 7:9
p: Deuteronomy 1 has the clearest proof text on the idea that there is an age of accountability. That children do not carry some original sin, as some insist falsely, but are innocent without the law.
p: This isn’t a set age, but a spiritual condition. For some, the realization between good and evil comes younger, some older.
callout: This is the comfort we have in the death of a young child. That they are with Christ in Heaven. [[2 Samuel 12:23]]

# from 6577
--- The wickedness of man
kicker: Genesis 6
big: Genesis 6:5
panel-warn: Not bloodlines | Many false doctrines place evil as something that is ‘other,’ foreign, introduced by bloodlines or genetics or ancestry.
panel: Man’s own heart | It is humanity that has fallen. It is man that is corrupt and wicked of heart. We are all one blood, given to the same temptation of the flesh, sinful nature, with free will and the need for salvation. [[Acts 17:26]]

=== The answer
# from 11083, 17871, 6854
--- Confessing we need saving
big: 1 John 1:8-9
p: You can’t get saved without this acknowledgment. You can’t accept salvation without knowing you need to be saved.
p: This pride and dishonesty, lying about sin to God, to others, even lying to ourselves, is the biggest stumbling block to accepting the Gospel.
note: We cannot acknowledge salvation without acknowledging what God is saving us from.

# from 11308, 6854
--- While we were yet sinners
scripture: Romans 6:23; Romans 5:8
p: We need salvation because we all sin. The punishment for sin is death and Hell. But the gift of God is eternal life in His Son. While we are sinners, Christ still died for us.
p: If we believe this in our hearts and trust on God’s promise, calling upon His holy name, we will be saved. That’s the Gospel. [[Romans 10:13]] [[1 John 2:2]]

=== Summary
# from 17714, 17503, 10736, 10792, 12858, 6577, 11083
--- Summary
point: All have sinned | We are all sinners before a holy God.
point: None righteous | There is none good but God. All have gone astray.
point: No difference | All are under sin. All deserve death and Hell. All need salvation. None have any excuse.
point: In our nature | There is no sin that follows man from birth, but only the understanding that it is in our nature that we still fall short.
point: Man’s own heart | It is man’s own wickedness that destroys us.
point: Confess it | You can’t accept salvation without knowing you need to be saved.

